        "Read the CREATE TABLE enrollments at the bottom of the file: its primary key tells you what one row is. In Q1, check what the WHERE must keep out (rows of other learners, and which status?) and what ORDER BY needs when two courses have the same title. For Q2, name the columns you insert into.",
        "A similar set of queries on lesson_progress (PRIMARY KEY (user_id, lesson_id)): list one learner's finished lessons with SELECT l.lesson_id, l.title FROM lesson_progress lp JOIN lessons l ON l.lesson_id = lp.lesson_id WHERE lp.user_id = :user_id AND lp.completed_at IS NOT NULL ORDER BY l.title, l.lesson_id; reset one lesson with UPDATE lesson_progress SET completed_at = NULL WHERE user_id = :user_id AND lesson_id = :lesson_id AND completed_at IS NOT NULL. Every column of the key is in the WHERE, plus the state the row must be in."
